## 8. Unsupported-input behavior (explicit bounds)

| Input | Behavior |
|---|---|
| CSV with malformed rows | default: error with full detail [S8]; opt-in: quarantine to ledger with ordinal/raw line; never silent [EXECUTED W2] |
| Row longer than engine max / pathological widths | engine error (`max_line_size` [S7]); our guard also bounds preview memory |
| Non-UTF-8/16/latin-1 encoding | declared out-of-band conversion; recorded as a transform [S7,S10] |
| Ambiguous timestamps | reject with message; require declared `timestampformat` [S7, CHOICE] |
| pandas-style whole-file load > RAM | size-guarded: refused with the declared bounded alternative (engine scan / chunked path); explicit different bound, per brief |
| 5 GB CSV aggregate/scan | engine bounded path — **target** [PROPOSED/UNEXECUTED V1] |
| Dataset changed since last hash | runs blocked until re-verified or re-registered; outputs go `stale` [EXECUTED W1] |
| Missing dataset on reopen | registered outputs `unverified`; external refs stay `unverified` by definition [CHOICE] |
| Two writers on one project | second writer refused with lock holder pid/boot-id [§4.6] |
| Engine version drift | engine pinned per project; reject counts/schema reports are engine-versioned facts [§3.5, CHOICE] |

