## 10. Critical dependencies and risks

- **DuckDB** (data contract anchor): fast-moving; CSV error semantics changed recently and more changes are pending [S12,S13,S15] — mitigate by pinning per project + permutation tests (V2). License MIT. [INFER on process]
- **nbformat/nbclient** (document/execution): stable, but the format is interchange-only and nbclient has no status model — our journal/status layer is the differentiator and our responsibility. [INFER]
- **OS sandbox availability**: bubblewrap is Linux; macOS/Windows need different primitives with weaker guarantees — the support boundary must say so per-OS rather than promise uniform isolation. [INFER vs S24]
- **jupyter-cache**: instructive but its invalidation story is aspirational by its own README [S6]; we adopt its *preconditions* and build the invalidation ourselves. Maintenance status of the project is a lead (L5).
- **endoflife.date** used as an aggregator for EOL dates [S22] — primary anchoring is the PEP set; a release process must re-verify at build time. [INFER]

